===Alternative spellings===
* [[chadar]], [[chaddar]], [[chuddar]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fa}} {{fa-Arab|[[چادر]]}} ''čâdor'', from {{etyl|sn}} {{term|sc=Deva|tr=chattram|lang=sa}} <ref>[http://www.bartleby.com/61/28/C0222800.html Chador in the American Heritage Dictionary of the English Language]</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[loose]] [[robe]], made from a single [[cloth]], worn as a [[combination]] [[head]] [[covering]], [[veil]] and [[shawl]] by [[Muslim]] [[women]], especially in [[Iran]].

